  // computeWordDiffV2 — keeps preview output consistent across tools.
  // CRITICAL: do NOT split keeping whitespace tokens — that produces
  // single-space "change" hunks that render as red+green noise.
  // Parse Word-emitted HTML into per-word formatting tokens via a
  // CHAR-STREAM walk: every character carries its bold/italic/underline
  // context from ancestor tags + inline styles. After walking, we
  // tokenize the reconstructed text by whitespace; a token's format is
  // "any char in it is bold/italic/underline". This handles Word's
  // common pattern of splitting a formatted word from its trailing
  // punctuation across sibling nodes (e.g. `<b>Provider</b>,` walks as
  // ["Provider"] then [","] — without char-stream we'd produce 2 tokens
  // for what `.text` correctly tokenizes as 1).
  //
  // Returns null on parse failure. Used ONLY by Show clause; AI rewrite
  // path doesn't set originalHtml so this is a no-op there.
  // Inline-style regexes anchor on `(?:^|[;\s])` to avoid false matches
  // on Word's `mso-bidi-font-weight: bold` properties.
